            <ArticleTitle>Neutrophil-mediated vascular barrier injury: Role of neutrophil extracellular traps.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/micc.12352</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Neutrophils play an essential role in host defense against infection or injury. While neutrophil activation is necessary for pathogen clearance and tissue repair, a hyperactive response can lead to tissue damage and microcirculatory disorders, a process involving complex neutrophil-endothelium cross talk. This review highlights recent research findings about neutrophil-mediated signaling and structural changes, including those induced by neutrophil extracellular traps, which ultimately lead to vascular barrier injury.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>© 2017 John Wiley &amp; Sons Ltd.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
